7. Important viva questions

Prepare these carefully. This experiment has many theory-based questions.

Q1. What is CI?

CI stands for Continuous Integration. It is the practice of frequently integrating code changes into a shared repository and automatically building and testing them.

Q2. What is CD?

CD stands for Continuous Delivery or Continuous Deployment. It automates the process of preparing or deploying software after integration and testing.

Q3. What is a CI/CD pipeline?

It is an automated sequence of steps used to build, test and deliver software.

Q4. What is Jenkins?

Jenkins is an open-source automation server used to automate software development tasks.

Q5. Why do we integrate Jenkins with GitHub?

To automatically retrieve source code from GitHub and build or test it using Jenkins.

Q6. What is a webhook?

A webhook is an automatic notification sent from one application to another when a particular event occurs.

Q7. What is GitHub integration?

It is connecting Jenkins with GitHub so Jenkins can access repositories and respond to code changes.

Q8. What is a build trigger?

A build trigger is an event or condition that starts a Jenkins build.

Q9. What is a pipeline?

A pipeline is a sequence of automated tasks involved in building, testing and delivering software.

Q10. What is a Jenkins plugin?

A plugin is an extension that adds additional functionality to Jenkins.

Q11. What is the Build Pipeline plugin?

It is a Jenkins plugin used to visualize the execution flow of jobs.

Q12. What is the purpose of Job1, Job2 and Job3?

They represent separate Jenkins jobs that can be organized into a build pipeline.

Q13. What happens when a developer pushes code to GitHub?

If webhook integration is configured correctly, GitHub sends a notification to Jenkins, which can trigger a build.

Q14. What is the difference between CI and CD?

CI focuses on integrating and testing code changes. CD focuses on preparing or deploying the tested application.

Q15. What is the purpose of */main?

It specifies that Jenkins should build the main branch.

Q16. What is source code management?

It is the process of tracking and managing changes to source code.

Q17. What is automated testing?

Automated testing uses software tools to execute test cases without manually performing every test.

Q18. What is the advantage of CI/CD?

It reduces manual work, detects errors early, speeds up software delivery and improves development efficiency.

Q19. Can Jenkins work without GitHub?

Yes. Jenkins can execute local programs and perform automation tasks without GitHub.

Q20. What is the difference between a job and a pipeline?

A job performs a configured task. A pipeline organizes multiple tasks or jobs into an execution workflow.

